@flexiarg process/spec-drift-by-displacement
@title T2: Spec or Plan Drift by Displacement, with No Decision
@keywords trap, T2, drift, displacement, spec-drift, jurisdictional-gap
@audience campaign operators, spec authors
@tone plain
@style pattern
@why war-room/wr-8-typed-files-are-sources-of-truth
@problem P-assured-process.md S1: the WM has no process spec at all yet, and the Lean spec precedent lost jurisdiction over failure paths by running only at close
@how a decision record authored by an actor before an operative artifact is replaced; checker jurisdiction over failure paths, not only success

! conclusion: When an operative artifact is replaced by another without any actor deciding to replace it, the plan has drifted by displacement. Repair is not archaeology but a refusing decision record: nothing replaces a typed source of truth without an author-authored decision, and the checker must hold jurisdiction over failure, where the hotfixes accumulate.

  + context: Dependency-ordered plans, Lean specifications, and any operative artifact others build against. Catalogued as T2 in N-process-trap-recording-conventions section 1.

  + IF:
    A spec or commissioned plan exists, and work continues beside it under a different, newer artifact.

  + HOWEVER:
    Archaeology finds momentum, seat deaths, and parked gates — no decision. The typed source of truth stops being one while still being cited as one.
    + VIOLATION (WM): the commissioned spine-first dependency-ordered build (2026-08-30) was displaced by an automatable closure ledger with no actor-authored decision performing the replacement. Receipt: futon2 holes DRIFT-2026-09-05-account.md:125, via N-process-trap-recording-conventions.md T2.
    + VIOLATION (APM): the Lean spec defines PhaseFailureClass and PhaseFailureDisposition with evidence-to-delayedRetry proven invalid, but the implementation grew a park sink across thirteen apparatus fault classes; claude-7 then added a FOURTH vocabulary (fault_taxonomy.clj) without reading the spec that had two — displacement committed by a well-intentioned repair.
    + SUB-MECHANISM (T2a, jurisdictional gap): drift goes where the checker is not — APM's checker had jurisdiction over success and none over failure. When diagnosing drift, first ask which region no instrument covers.

  + THEN:
    Require an author-authored decision record before any operative artifact is replaced, and give the checker jurisdiction over failure paths as well as success paths; when diagnosing drift, locate the uncovered region before asking who decided what.

  + BECAUSE:
    Displacement is usually committed by repair, not by sabotage; only a refusing boundary between "the spec changed" and "a file changed" can tell them apart.
    + evidence: N-process-trap-recording-conventions.md section 1, T2 and T2a, three receipts. Authority grounding: WR-8, typed files are sources of truth — the violation is precisely a typed file ceasing to be the source of truth without decision.
